WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:11.922
Hi! You leave home at 7:35 in the morning. What does the clock look like? Today we'll tell the time to the minute and change hours to minutes.

2
00:00:12.072 --> 00:00:17.346
On a clock, the short hand shows the hour and the long hand shows the minutes.

3
00:00:17.496 --> 00:00:22.362
When the minute hand moves from one number to the next, 5 minutes pass.

4
00:00:22.512 --> 00:00:27.402
The minute hand on 7 means 7 fives, 35 minutes.

5
00:00:27.552 --> 00:00:34.218
The hour hand is just past 7 and not yet at 8, so it's 7:35.

6
00:00:34.368 --> 00:00:39.066
One full turn of the minute hand is 60 minutes, which is 1 hour.

7
00:00:39.216 --> 00:00:42.018
Half an hour is 30 minutes.

8
00:00:42.168 --> 00:00:47.130
1 hour 20 minutes is 60 plus 20, which is 80 minutes.

9
00:00:47.280 --> 00:00:53.010
We use a.m. for the morning, and p.m. for the afternoon and night.

10
00:00:53.160 --> 00:00:59.562
Watch out! Many pupils think 1 hour is 100 minutes. That's wrong!

11
00:00:59.712 --> 00:01:05.346
The minute hand goes round once in 60 minutes, so 1 hour is 60 minutes.

12
00:01:05.496 --> 00:01:10.602
When you change hours to minutes, always use 60.

13
00:01:10.752 --> 00:01:20.826
Your turn! The minute hand points to 4. How many minutes past the hour? Pause and think.

14
00:01:20.976 --> 00:01:26.994
4 fives are 20, so 20 minutes. Did you get it right?

15
00:01:27.144 --> 00:01:38.154
Another one! The hour hand is past 3 and the minute hand is on 9. What time is it? Pause and think.

16
00:01:38.304 --> 00:01:45.186
9 fives are 45, so it's 3:45. Did you get it right?

17
00:01:45.336 --> 00:01:53.826
Here's another! How many minutes are there in 2 hours? Pause and think.

18
00:01:53.976 --> 00:02:00.762
60 plus 60 is 120 minutes. Did you get it right?

19
00:02:00.912 --> 00:02:09.882
Try one more! How many hours and minutes are 90 minutes? Pause and think.

20
00:02:10.032 --> 00:02:17.610
90 minus 60 leaves 30, so 1 hour 30 minutes. Did you get it right?

21
00:02:17.760 --> 00:02:27.690
Try one more! What time is it 25 minutes after 7:35? Pause and think.

22
00:02:27.840 --> 00:02:35.538
35 plus 25 is 60 minutes, so it's 8 o'clock. Did you get it right?

23
00:02:35.688 --> 00:02:44.826
Last one! Dinner at 7 in the evening: a.m. or p.m.? Pause and think.

24
00:02:44.976 --> 00:02:51.330
Evening uses p.m., so 7 p.m. Did you get it right?

25
00:02:51.480 --> 00:03:01.266
Remember: the short hand shows hours and the long hand shows minutes. One number on the clock is 5 minutes, and 1 hour is 60 minutes.

26
00:03:01.416 --> 00:03:06.714
Before you go out today, look at a clock and say the time!

